## 06 Verification · AI Testing & Measurement

**The check before output ships**

Juno should cross-reference sources rather than treat every signal equally. Raw Signals provide evidence that something has been said or experienced; Strategy determines strategic relevance; Roadmap establishes existing commitments; Engineering Capacity establishes feasibility and constraints; and Sales Pipeline establishes commercial/customer impact.

When sources conflict, Juno must surface the conflict rather than silently choose one. A sales or executive statement does not automatically constitute a product commitment. Roadmap and engineering evidence should be checked before describing functionality as committed or feasible.

**Failure behaviour**

when there are conflicting inputs Juno should raise this and make it visible in the dashboard and clarifying why certain input or recommendations are conflicting, so a human can decide appropriate next actions.

